{"format_version": 2, "segments": [{"kind": "text", "text": " ὀφθαλμός, ὁ, (ὄπωπ-α, ὀφ-θῆναι, v. ὄψ B) eye, used by "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hom.", "author_abbreviation": "Hom.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": " and "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hes.", "author_abbreviation": "Hes.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": " mostly in pl.; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ὀφθαλμοὶ δ' ὡς εἰ κέρα ἕστασαν . . ἀτρέμας ἐν βλεφάροισι Od. 19.211", "author_abbreviation": "Od.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": sg., παίειν τινὰ ἐς τὸν ὀ. "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hdt. 9.22", "author_abbreviation": "Hdt.", "tlg_author": "0016", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": the pl. continued most common, but the dual also occurs, as in "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Ar. Nu. 362", "author_abbreviation": "Ar.", "tlg_author": "0019", "tlg_work": "003", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": pl. is used in many phrases, ἐλθέμεν ἐς ὀφθαλμούς τινος before one's eyes, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Il. 24.204", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; οὐδ' Ἀχιλῆος ὀφθαλμοὺς εἴσειμι ib."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "463", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; ὀφθαλμοῖσιν ἰδεῖν, ὁρᾶσθαι, etc., "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "10.275", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Od. 4.47", "author_abbreviation": "Od.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", etc.; but ἐν ὀφθαλμοῖσιν ὁρᾶν, νοεῖν, to see before one's eyes, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "8.459", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Il. 24.312", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; ἔχειν ἐν ὀ. to have before one's eyes, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "X. An. 4.5.29", "author_abbreviation": "X.", "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "006", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; τὰ ἐν ὀ. what is before one's eyes, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Pl. Tht. 174c", "author_abbreviation": "Pl.", "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "006", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; τὸ ἐν τοῖς ὀ. δὴ γελοῖον what was ridiculous to the eye, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Id. R. 452d", "author_abbreviation": "Id.", "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "030", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; ἐπίπροσθε τῶν ὀ. "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Id. Smp. 213a", "author_abbreviation": "Id.", "tlg_author": "0059", "tlg_work": "011", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "πρὸ τῶν ὀ. προφαίνεσθαι Aeschin. 2.148", "author_abbreviation": "Aeschin.", "tlg_author": "0026", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ἐπ' ὀφθαλμῶν Luc. Tox. 20", "author_abbreviation": "Luc.", "tlg_author": "0062", "tlg_work": "044", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; γενέσθαι τινὶ ἐξ ὀφθαλμῶν to get out of any one's sight, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hdt. 5.106", "author_abbreviation": "Hdt.", "tlg_author": "0016", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ἐξ ὀ. ἀποπέμψασθαι Id. 1.120", "author_abbreviation": "Id.", "tlg_author": "0016", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ἐξ ὀ. ποιεῖν Alciphr. 3.20", "author_abbreviation": "Alciphr.", "tlg_author": "0640", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; κατ' ὀφθαλμοὺς λέγειν τινί to tell one to one's face, opp. εἰς οὖς, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Ar. Ra. 626", "author_abbreviation": "Ar.", "tlg_author": "0019", "tlg_work": "009", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; τυράννου κατ' ὀ. κατηγορεῖν to accuse him to his face, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "X. Hier. 1.14", "author_abbreviation": "X.", "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "008", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": sg. in the phrase πρὸς ὀφθαλμὸν ἐπιχεῖν, μίσγειν, by eye, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "PHolm. 7.23", "author_abbreviation": "PHolm.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "PLeid.X. 62", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; eyes were painted on the bows of vessels, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "βλοσυροῖς κατὰ πρῷραν ὀφθαλμοῖς οἷον βλέπει Philostr. Im. 1.19", "author_abbreviation": "Philostr.", "tlg_author": "1600", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", cf. "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "IG 22.1607.24", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Poll. 1.86", "author_abbreviation": "Poll.", "tlg_author": "0542", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; whence the joke in "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Ar. Ach. 97", "author_abbreviation": "Ar.", "tlg_author": "0019", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ". στέρησις ὀφθαλμῶν temporary loss of sight, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Gal. 17(1).400", "author_abbreviation": "Gal.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ". in sg., the eye of a master or ruler, πάντα ἰδὼν Διὸς ὀ. "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hes. Op. 267", "author_abbreviation": "Hes.", "tlg_author": "0020", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Δίκης ὀ. ὃς τὰ πάνθ' ὁρᾷ Men. Mon. 179", "author_abbreviation": "Men.", "tlg_author": "0541", "tlg_work": "047", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "δεσπότου ὀ. X. Oec. 12.20", "author_abbreviation": "X.", "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "003", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; ἀκοίμητος ὀ., of God, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Secund. Sent. 3", "author_abbreviation": "Secund.", "tlg_author": "1521", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; so a king is called "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ὀ. οἴκων A. Ch. 934", "author_abbreviation": "A.", "tlg_author": "0085", "tlg_work": "006", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": " (so "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "ὄμμα Pers. 169", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0085", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "); and in Persia ὀφθαλμὸς βασιλέως the king's eye was a confidential officer, through whom he beheld his kingdom and subjects, "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "A. Pers. 979", "author_abbreviation": "A.", "tlg_author": "0085", "tlg_work": "002", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(lyr.), "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hdt. 1.114", "author_abbreviation": "Hdt.", "tlg_author": "0016", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Ar. Ach. 92", "author_abbreviation": "Ar.", "tlg_author": "0019", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "X. Cyr. 8.2.10", "author_abbreviation": "X.", "tlg_author": "0032", "tlg_work": "007", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": " sq., "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Arist. Pol. 1287b29", "author_abbreviation": "Arist.", "tlg_author": "0086", "tlg_work": "035", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Ph. 1.642", "autho